    page('learning/leading-transformation','Leading Transformation: two dated learning routes','<p>Leading Transformation is the Public Service Transformation Academy’s programme. RedQuadrant’s Tool Shed is a supported practitioner learning and application offer using related content. The original 24-module architecture is retained here alongside the revised route agreed on 6 September 2026.</p><p><a href="https://www.publicservicetransformation.org/programmes/leading-transformation/">Leading Transformation programme</a> · <a href="https://www.redquadrant.com/toolshed/">RedQuadrant Tool Shed</a></p><h2>Revised route: 6 September 2026</h2><p>The five worlds are perspectives with cross-links: leadership and political; citizen; service; management; learning and change. Five Core Practices recur throughout. Live work begins in module 3, service prototyping in module 12, and the Four Dynamics are introduced in module 4 and applied in module 18. The final simulation requires a substantial delivery block and hundred-day follow-through.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Focus and world</th><th>Practice</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+current_rows+'</tbody></table><h2>Original route: 2020–2025 source versions</h2><p>The final column is an AI-assisted editorial correspondence between the public summaries. It helps readers find material across versions; it does not claim formal equivalence. New emphases include explicit relational public services, digital/data/AI judgement, and the Four Dynamics.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Original module</th><th>Title and content</th><th>Related revised modules</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+legacy_rows+'</tbody></table><h2>Follow the concepts</h2><p><a href="/#view=item&amp;id=method_or_methodology_viable_system_model_vsm">Viable System Model</a> · <a href="/#view=item&amp;id=intervention_skill_lean_and_six_sigma">Lean: operational learning</a> · <a href="/#view=item&amp;id=method_or_methodology_patterns_of_strategy">Patterns of Strategy</a> · <a href="/#view=item&amp;id=intervention_skill_appreciative_inquiry">Appreciative Inquiry</a></p><p>The source register distinguishes dated curriculum facts from these editorial connections. A module sequence does not establish intellectual influence. Core learning, optional depth, supported application and demonstrated competence remain different things. See the programme providers for current arrangements.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://github.com/antlerboy/PSTA/blob/main/content/leading-transformation.json">Original public module register</a> and <a href="https://github.com/antlerboy/PSTA/blob/main/content/curriculum-2026.json">Revised public module register</a>. Prepared with AI assistance; independent specialist review is not recorded.</p>')
