    page('corpora/ing-ocad','David Ing’s OCAD reading route','<p class="note">This guide covers the six core resources in the supplied recommendation. The complete <a href="'+next(s['url'] for s in d['sources'] if s['id']==ocad)+'">13-week course pro forma</a> could not be retrieved for this pass. A module-by-module guide and close reading of its additional papers remain open.</p><p>The recommendation identifies Stephen N. Davies as the winter 2026 course instructor and David Ing as a volunteer contributor. These are distinct roles.</p><h2>Follow the readings</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Resource</th><th>What has been checked</th><th>Connection</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+rows+'</tbody></table><h2>One explicit comparison</h2><p>Reynolds and Holwell’s introductory abstract compares SD, VSM, SODA, SSM and CSH. Its rationale concerns change and uncertainty, constructivist use, and combinations of methods. <a href="https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4471-7472-1_1">Read the chapter abstract and access options</a>. This is abstract-level evidence, not a claim to have read the subscription chapter.</p><h2>How to read the connections</h2><p>Selection for teaching, authorship, a conceptual comparison and historical influence are different statements. The map records which kind is being made. A course’s order is not evidence that one author influenced the next.</p><p>Prepared with AI assistance from named sources. Evaluations and proposed practice uses remain editorial contributions, open to correction. No contributor role or independent review is implied.</p>')
